+**The lead's note for this run (beta, 2026-10-23).** You run in your own git worktree. First `git fetch origin claude/stoic-ride-54ddxp && git checkout --detach origin/claude/stoic-ride-54ddxp`; the lead will tell you when fix wave 5's last batch lands, and you then move to that head. Symlink today's crawl: `ln -s /tmp/claude-0/-home-user-melon-seek/b6b764de-866b-5af7-92f3-f582ebca24d9/scratchpad/wt-data2/data/snapshots data/snapshots; mkdir -p data/beta; ln -s /tmp/claude-0/-home-user-melon-seek/b6b764de-866b-5af7-92f3-f582ebca24d9/scratchpad/wt-data2/data/beta/snapshots data/beta/snapshots`, and `ln -s /home/user/melon-seek/node_modules node_modules`. Never commit those links, and **never move them**: an agent hung twice on moving a data link. For the CI-like `npm test` use a clean checkout with no links (`git worktree add --detach /tmp/claude-0/-home-user-melon-seek/b6b764de-866b-5af7-92f3-f582ebca24d9/scratchpad/qa-suite-beta/clean HEAD`, link node_modules, `MELON_BETA_SNAPSHOT_DIR= timeout 1200 npm test`).
+
